    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d809">

                <pb facs="0941" n="931" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg931"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/2218½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Roosevelt to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-10">July 10, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The impression which the Polish Ambassador received<anchor n="73"
                        xml:id="d809-f1"/> is, of course, utterly contrary to the fact. In my talk
                    with General Sikorski and the Ambassador I spoke of food as a weapon in the
                    actual war. The <pb facs="0942" n="932" xml:id="pg932"/> only other thing I said
                    was that it was obvious that after the war food would go by priority to the
                    people of our Allies—the United Nations—ahead of food to feed people in Germany.
                    That statement is, of course, obvious.</p>
                <p>I hope you will take the matter up with the Polish Ambassador.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ranklin</hi>] D. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
